module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFinite.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.Basic

/-!
# Trimming the generators of a quasi-coherent module on an affine open

This file proves the affine step of [Stacks, Tag 01PF]. Let `F` be a quasi-coherent
`𝒪_X`-module, let `V` be an affine open of `X` and let `W ≤ V` be a quasi-compact open on which
`F` has finite-type sections. Then **finitely many** sections of `F` over `V` already generate
`F` over every affine open contained in `W`.

In the source this is the last paragraph of the proof of Tag 01PF: on `X = Spec R` with
`F = Ñ`, the quasi-compact open `W` is covered by finitely many `D(f_i)` with `N_{f_i}`
finitely generated by Tag 01PB, and the submodule `N' ⊆ N` generated by numerators of those
generators satisfies `N'_{f_i} = N_{f_i}`, hence `Ñ'|_W = Ñ|_W`.

The conclusion is stated as a *spanning* statement over the affine opens inside `W`, because
that is the datum `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.IsCompatible` consumes: a
quasi-coherent subsheaf of `F` is a family of submodules of the sections over the affine opens,
and the subsheaf cut out by the span of a finite set of sections of `F` over `V` agrees with `F`
over `W` exactly when that span is everything on each affine open inside `W`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffine.finite_sections_le`: [Stacks, Tag 01PB] relative to
  an open `W`. If `F` is quasi-coherent and has finitely many generating sections near every
  point of `W`, then `Γ(F, Z)` is a finite `Γ(X, Z)`-module for **every** affine open `Z ≤ W`.
  This generalizes `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFinite.finite_sections`, which is the case
  `W = ⊤`, and is what makes the hypothesis of the main result checkable from a finite-type
  hypothesis that only holds over `W`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffine.span_restrict_eq_top_of_le`: a set of sections over
  an affine open which spans the sections over an affine open `Z` spans the sections over every
  affine open inside `Z`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffine.mem_span_restrict_of_cover`: membership in the span of
  a set of sections restricted from a larger open is local on an affine open. This is
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.mem_of_cover` for a span family, which needs no
  compatibility hypothesis because the family of spans is automatically compatible.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffine.exists_finite_spanning_subset`: **the affine step of
  [Stacks, Tag 01PF]**, as described above.

## Implementation notes

No stacks attribute is attached. Tag 01PF is a single assertion about an arbitrary
quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme; what is proved here is the affine case of its last
reduction, so the covering set of the tag is not complete and the tag is withheld. The two
further steps the source takes — the extension of a quasi-coherent subsheaf across a
quasi-compact open immersion, which is [Stacks, Tag 01PE] and is available as
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_quasicoherentSubobject_restrict`, and the induction over a finite
affine covering gluing the results together — are not in this file.

The passage from "spans over each member of a finite cover of `Z` by basic opens" to "spans
over `Z`" is `Submodule.eq_top_of_isLocalized₀_span`, applied exactly as in
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.mem_of_cover`: over a basic open of an affine open the
sections of a quasi-coherent module are the corresponding localization of the sections, by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.isLocalizedModule_restrictₗ`, and a submodule
whose every localization along a spanning family is everything is everything.

Lifting generators from `Γ(F, X.basicOpen a)` back to `Γ(F, V)` does not need the localization:
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.exists_finite_subset_span` already produces, for a
single section over a smaller affine open, a finite set of sections over the larger one whose
restrictions generate it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PE)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits SheafOfModules TopologicalSpace Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffine

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFinite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### Tag 01PB relative to an open -/

/-- The elements of `t` span the unit ideal of an affine open `U` as soon as the basic opens they
cut out cover `U`. -/
private theorem span_eq_top_of_forall_mem_basicOpen {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (t : Set Γ(X, U)) (h : ∀ x ∈ U, ∃ g ∈ t, x ∈ X.basicOpen g) : Ideal.span t = ⊤ := by
  rw [← hU.self_le_iSup_basicOpen_iff]
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hxg⟩ := h x hx
  exact Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨g, hg⟩, hxg⟩

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 01PB] relative to an open `W`.** If a quasi-coherent module `F` has finitely
many generating sections near every point of an open `W`, then its sections over every affine
open contained in `W` form a finite module.

This is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFinite.finite_sections` with its global finite-type
hypothesis localized to `W`; the proof is the same, since that one only ever uses generating
sections near the points of the affine open it is applied to. The case `W = ⊤` recovers it. -/
theorem finite_sections_le (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] {W : X.Opens}
    (hloc : ∀ x ∈ W, ∃ (Z : X.Opens) (_ : x ∈ Z) (σ : (F.restrict Z.ι).GeneratingSections),
      Finite σ.I)
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hUW : U ≤ W) :
    Module.Finite Γ(X, U) Γ(F, U) := by
  set t : Set Γ(X, U) := {g | Module.Finite Γ(X, X.basicOpen g) Γ(F, X.basicOpen g)} with ht
  have hspan : Ideal.span t = ⊤ := by
    refine span_eq_top_of_forall_mem_basicOpen hU t fun x hx => ?_
    obtain ⟨Z, hxZ, σ, hσ⟩ := hloc x (hUW hx)
    obtain ⟨g, hgZ, hxg⟩ := hU.exists_basicOpen_le (⟨x, hxZ⟩ : Z) hx
    have hfin : Finite (generatingSectionsRestrictLE F hgZ σ).I := hσ
    exact ⟨g, @finite_sections_of_generatingSections _ F _ _ (hU.basicOpen g)
      (generatingSectionsRestrictLE F hgZ σ) hfin, hxg⟩
  let _ : ∀ g : t, Algebra Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen (g : Γ(X, U))) :=
    fun g => algebraOfLE X (X.basicOpen_le (g : Γ(X, U)))
  let _ : ∀ g : t, IsLocalization.Away (g : Γ(X, U)) Γ(X, X.basicOpen (g : Γ(X, U))) :=
    fun _ => hU.isLocalization_basicOpen _
  let _ : ∀ g : t, Module Γ(X, U) Γ(F, X.basicOpen (g : Γ(X, U))) :=
    fun g => moduleOfLE F (X.basicOpen_le (g : Γ(X, U)))
  let _ : ∀ g : t, IsScalarTower Γ(X, U) Γ(X, X.basicOpen (g : Γ(X, U)))
      Γ(F, X.basicOpen (g : Γ(X, U))) :=
    fun g => isScalarTowerOfLE F (X.basicOpen_le (g : Γ(X, U)))
  let _ : ∀ g : t, IsLocalizedModule.Away (g : Γ(X, U))
      (restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le (g : Γ(X, U)))) :=
    fun _ => isLocalizedModule_restrictₗ F hU _ rfl _
  exact Module.Finite.of_localizationSpan' t hspan
    (fun g => restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le (g : Γ(X, U)))) (fun g => g.2)

/-! ### Spanning descends along inclusions of affine opens -/

/-- Restricting a family of sections of `F` over an affine open `V` to an affine open `Z ≤ V`
and then further to an affine open `Z' ≤ Z` is restricting it to `Z'` in one step. -/
theorem image_res_res (F : X.Modules) {V Z Z' : X.Opens} (hZV : Z ≤ V) (hZ'Z : Z' ≤ Z)
    (A : Set Γ(F, V)) :
    F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hZ'Z).op '' (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hZV).op '' A) =
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hZ'Z.trans hZV)).op '' A := by
  rw [Set.image_image]
  exact Set.image_congr' fun x => res_res F hZV hZ'Z x

/-- The `Γ(X, V)`-linear restriction map of `F` is the restriction map of the underlying
presheaf. -/
theorem restrictₗ_apply (F : X.Modules) {U V : X.Opens} (h : U ≤ V) (x : Γ(F, V)) :
    letI := moduleOfLE F h
    restrictₗ F h x = F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op x :=
  rfl

/-- Membership in the span of restricted sections of an affine open `Z` can be checked after
restricting to the basic opens `X.basicOpen c`, for `c` in a set `u` spanning the unit ideal. -/
private theorem mem_span_restrict_of_forall_basicOpen (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    {V Z : X.Opens} (hZ : IsAffineOpen Z) (hZV : Z ≤ V) (B : Set Γ(F, V)) (s : Γ(F, Z))
    (u : Set Γ(X, Z)) (hu : Ideal.span u = ⊤)
    (h : ∀ c ∈ u, F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le c)).op s ∈
      Submodule.span Γ(X, X.basicOpen c)
        (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE ((X.basicOpen_le c).trans hZV)).op '' B)) :
    s ∈ Submodule.span Γ(X, Z) (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hZV).op '' B) := by
  let _ : ∀ c : u, Algebra Γ(X, Z) Γ(X, X.basicOpen (c : Γ(X, Z))) :=
    fun c => algebraOfLE X (X.basicOpen_le (c : Γ(X, Z)))
  let _ : ∀ c : u, IsLocalization.Away (c : Γ(X, Z)) Γ(X, X.basicOpen (c : Γ(X, Z))) :=
    fun _ => hZ.isLocalization_basicOpen _
  let _ : ∀ c : u, Module Γ(X, Z) Γ(F, X.basicOpen (c : Γ(X, Z))) :=
    fun c => moduleOfLE F (X.basicOpen_le (c : Γ(X, Z)))
  let _ : ∀ c : u, IsScalarTower Γ(X, Z) Γ(X, X.basicOpen (c : Γ(X, Z)))
      Γ(F, X.basicOpen (c : Γ(X, Z))) :=
    fun c => isScalarTowerOfLE F (X.basicOpen_le (c : Γ(X, Z)))
  let _ : ∀ c : u, IsLocalizedModule.Away (c : Γ(X, Z))
      (restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le (c : Γ(X, Z)))) :=
    fun _ => isLocalizedModule_restrictₗ F hZ _ rfl _
  refine Submodule.mem_of_isLocalized_span u hu
    (fun c => Γ(F, X.basicOpen (c : Γ(X, Z))))
    (fun c => restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le (c : Γ(X, Z)))) fun c => ?_
  have key : Submodule.localized₀ (Submonoid.powers (c : Γ(X, Z)))
      (restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le (c : Γ(X, Z))))
        (Submodule.span Γ(X, Z) (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hZV).op '' B)) =
      (Submodule.span Γ(X, X.basicOpen (c : Γ(X, Z)))
        (restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le (c : Γ(X, Z))) ''
          ((Submodule.span Γ(X, Z) (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hZV).op '' B) :
            Submodule Γ(X, Z) Γ(F, Z)) : Set Γ(F, Z)))).restrictScalars Γ(X, Z) := by
    rw [← Submodule.restrictScalars_localized' Γ(X, X.basicOpen (c : Γ(X, Z))),
      Submodule.localized'_eq_span]
  rw [key, Submodule.restrictScalars_mem,
    Set.image_congr' fun x => restrictₗ_apply F (X.basicOpen_le (c : Γ(X, Z))) x,
    span_image_span F (X.basicOpen_le (c : Γ(X, Z)))
      (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hZV).op '' B),
    image_res_res F hZV (X.basicOpen_le (c : Γ(X, Z))) B]
  exact h c c.2

/-- **Spanning descends.** If the restrictions of `A ⊆ Γ(F, V)` span the sections of `F` over an
affine open `Z ≤ V`, they span the sections over every affine open `Z' ≤ Z`.

The sections over `Z'` are generated over `Γ(X, Z')` by the restrictions of the sections over
`Z` — that is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.span_range_restrict_eq_top`, the
surjectivity half of [Stacks, Tag 01I9] — so it suffices to spread the span over `Z` out to
`Z'`, which is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.span_image_span`. -/
theorem span_restrict_eq_top_of_le (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] {V Z Z' : X.Opens}
    (hZ : IsAffineOpen Z) (hZ' : IsAffineOpen Z') (hZV : Z ≤ V) (hZ'Z : Z' ≤ Z)
    (A : Set Γ(F, V))
    (h : Submodule.span Γ(X, Z) (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hZV).op '' A) = ⊤) :
    Submodule.span Γ(X, Z') (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hZ'Z.trans hZV)).op '' A) = ⊤ := by
  have key := span_image_span F hZ'Z (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hZV).op '' A)
  rw [h, image_res_res F hZV hZ'Z A] at key
  rw [← key]
  have hcoe : ((⊤ : Submodule Γ(X, Z) Γ(F, Z)) : Set Γ(F, Z)) = Set.univ := by
    ext x; simp
  rw [hcoe, Set.image_univ]
  exact span_range_restrict_eq_top F hZ hZ' hZ'Z

/-! ### Membership in the span of restricted sections is local -/

/-- **Membership in the span of a set of restricted sections is local.** Let `F` be
quasi-coherent, let `B` be a set of sections of `F` over an open `V`, and let `Z ≤ V` be an
affine open. A section of `F` over `Z` which, on an affine open neighbourhood of each of its
points inside `Z`, lies in the span of the restrictions of `B`, already lies in the span of the
restrictions of `B` over `Z`.

This is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.mem_of_cover` for the particular family of
submodules spanned by the restrictions of a fixed set of sections, and unlike that lemma it
needs no compatibility hypothesis: the family of spans *is* compatible, by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.span_image_span`. Note also that `V` is not required to
be affine. -/
theorem mem_span_restrict_of_cover (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] {V Z : X.Opens}
    (hZ : IsAffineOpen Z) (hZV : Z ≤ V) (B : Set Γ(F, V)) (s : Γ(F, Z))
    (hcov : ∀ x ∈ Z, ∃ (Z' : X.Opens) (_ : IsAffineOpen Z') (h : Z' ≤ Z), x ∈ Z' ∧
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op s ∈
        Submodule.span Γ(X, Z') (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h.trans hZV)).op '' B)) :
    s ∈ Submodule.span Γ(X, Z) (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hZV).op '' B) := by
  classical
  -- Spanning the restrictions of `B` is inherited by any smaller affine open.
  have hdown : ∀ (Z' Z'' : X.Opens) (h' : Z' ≤ Z) (h'' : Z'' ≤ Z'),
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h').op s ∈
          Submodule.span Γ(X, Z') (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h'.trans hZV)).op '' B) →
        F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h''.trans h')).op s ∈
          Submodule.span Γ(X, Z'')
            (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE ((h''.trans h').trans hZV)).op '' B) := by
    intro Z' Z'' h' h'' hmem
    have hstep : F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h'').op (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h').op s) ∈
        Submodule.span Γ(X, Z'') (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h'').op ''
          ((Submodule.span Γ(X, Z') (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h'.trans hZV)).op '' B) :
            Submodule Γ(X, Z') Γ(F, Z')) : Set Γ(F, Z'))) :=
      Submodule.subset_span ⟨_, hmem, rfl⟩
    rw [span_image_span F h'' (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h'.trans hZV)).op '' B),
      image_res_res F (h'.trans hZV) h'' B] at hstep
    rwa [res_res F h' h'' s] at hstep
  -- The basic opens of `Z` on which the span contains the restriction of `s` cover `Z`.
  set u : Set Γ(X, Z) := {a | F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le a)).op s ∈
    Submodule.span Γ(X, X.basicOpen a)
      (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE ((X.basicOpen_le a).trans hZV)).op '' B)} with hu
  have huspan : Ideal.span u = ⊤ := by
    refine span_eq_top_of_forall_mem_basicOpen hZ u fun x hx => ?_
    obtain ⟨Z', hZ'aff, h', hxZ', hmem⟩ := hcov x hx
    obtain ⟨a, ha1, ha2⟩ := hZ.exists_basicOpen_le (⟨x, hxZ'⟩ : Z') hx
    exact ⟨a, hdown Z' (X.basicOpen a) h' ha1 hmem, ha2⟩
  exact mem_span_restrict_of_forall_basicOpen F hZ hZV B s u huspan fun c hc => hc

/-! ### The affine step of Tag 01PF -/

/-- **The affine step of [Stacks, Tag 01PF].** Let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module, `V` an
affine open of `X` and `W ≤ V` a quasi-compact open such that the sections of `F` over every
affine open inside `W` form a finite module — by `finite_sections_le` this last hypothesis is
[Stacks, Tag 01PB] applied to a finite-type hypothesis holding only over `W`. Then there is a
**finite** set `A` of sections of `F` over `V` whose restrictions generate the sections of `F`
over every affine open contained in `W`.

Equivalently: the quasi-coherent subsheaf of `F|_V` generated by the finitely many sections `A`
already agrees with `F` over `W`. This is the source's `N' ⊆ N` with `N'_{f_i} = N_{f_i}`.

`W` is covered by finitely many basic opens `X.basicOpen a` of `V` contained in `W`, by
quasi-compactness and because the basic opens of an affine open form a basis. On each of them
the sections form a finite module, so finitely many sections generate them; each generator is a
`Γ(X, X.basicOpen a)`-combination of restrictions of finitely many sections over `V` by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.exists_finite_subset_span`, and `A` collects all of
those. Spanning then holds over every affine open inside one of the chosen basic opens by
`span_restrict_eq_top_of_le`, and over an arbitrary affine `Z ≤ W` by the local nature of
spanning along the cover of `Z` by the basic opens cut out on it. -/
theorem exists_finite_spanning_subset (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] {V W : X.Opens}
    (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (hWV : W ≤ V) (hW : IsCompact (W : Set X))
    (hfin : ∀ Z : X.Opens, IsAffineOpen Z → Z ≤ W → Module.Finite Γ(X, Z) Γ(F, Z)) :
    ∃ A : Set Γ(F, V), A.Finite ∧ ∀ (Z : X.Opens), IsAffineOpen Z → ∀ h : Z ≤ W,
      Submodule.span Γ(X, Z) (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h.trans hWV)).op '' A) = ⊤ := by
  classical
  -- A finite set of basic opens of `V`, each inside `W`, covering `W`.
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hW.elim_finite_subcover
    (fun a : {a : Γ(X, V) // X.basicOpen a ≤ W} => (X.basicOpen a.1 : Set X))
    (fun a => (X.basicOpen a.1).isOpen) (by
      intro x hx
      obtain ⟨a, ha1, ha2⟩ := hV.exists_basicOpen_le (⟨x, hx⟩ : W) (hWV hx)
      exact Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨⟨a, ha1⟩, ha2⟩)
  -- Over each of those basic opens, finitely many sections over `V` already span.
  have hstep : ∀ a : {a : Γ(X, V) // X.basicOpen a ≤ W}, ∃ B : Set Γ(F, V), B.Finite ∧
      Submodule.span Γ(X, X.basicOpen a.1)
        (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (a.2.trans hWV)).op '' B) = ⊤ := by
    intro a
    have haff : IsAffineOpen (X.basicOpen a.1) := hV.basicOpen a.1
    have hfa : Module.Finite Γ(X, X.basicOpen a.1) Γ(F, X.basicOpen a.1) := hfin _ haff a.2
    obtain ⟨n, g, hg⟩ := Module.Finite.exists_fin (R := Γ(X, X.basicOpen a.1))
      (M := Γ(F, X.basicOpen a.1))
    choose B hBfin hBspan using fun i : Fin n =>
      exists_finite_subset_span F ⟨V, hV⟩ ⟨X.basicOpen a.1, haff⟩ (g i)
    refine ⟨⋃ i, B i, Set.finite_iUnion hBfin, ?_⟩
    rw [eq_top_iff, ← hg, Submodule.span_le]
    rintro y ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact Submodule.span_mono (Set.image_mono (Set.subset_iUnion B i))
      (hBspan i (a.2.trans hWV))
  choose B hBfin hBspan using hstep
  refine ⟨⋃ a ∈ (s : Set {a : Γ(X, V) // X.basicOpen a ≤ W}), B a,
    s.finite_toSet.biUnion fun a _ => hBfin a, ?_⟩
  set A : Set Γ(F, V) := ⋃ a ∈ (s : Set {a : Γ(X, V) // X.basicOpen a ≤ W}), B a with hA
  -- `A` spans over each chosen basic open, and hence over every affine open inside one.
  have hAspan : ∀ a ∈ s, Submodule.span Γ(X, X.basicOpen (a : {a : Γ(X, V) // _}).1)
      (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE ((a : {a : Γ(X, V) // _}).2.trans hWV)).op '' A) = ⊤ := by
    intro a ha
    rw [eq_top_iff, ← hBspan a]
    exact Submodule.span_mono (Set.image_mono (Set.subset_biUnion_of_mem ha))
  intro Z hZ hZW
  -- The basic opens of `Z` cut out by the chosen `a` cover `Z`; spanning is local along them.
  set r : {a : Γ(X, V) // X.basicOpen a ≤ W} → Γ(X, Z) :=
    fun a => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hZW.trans hWV)).op a.1 with hr
  set u : Set Γ(X, Z) := r '' (s : Set {a : Γ(X, V) // X.basicOpen a ≤ W}) with hu
  have hbo : ∀ a : {a : Γ(X, V) // X.basicOpen a ≤ W},
      X.basicOpen (r a) = Z ⊓ X.basicOpen a.1 := fun a => Scheme.basicOpen_res _ _ _
  have huspan : Ideal.span u = ⊤ := by
    refine span_eq_top_of_forall_mem_basicOpen hZ u fun x hx => ?_
    obtain ⟨a, ha, hxa⟩ : ∃ a ∈ s, x ∈ (X.basicOpen a.1 : Set X) := by
      have := hs (hZW hx)
      simpa using this
    exact ⟨r a, ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩, by rw [hbo a]; exact ⟨hx, hxa⟩⟩
  -- Over each basic open of `Z` in the cover, `A` spans, because it spans one step up.
  refine eq_top_iff.2 fun t _ => mem_span_restrict_of_forall_basicOpen F hZ (hZW.trans hWV) A t
    u huspan fun c hc => ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha, hac⟩ := hc
  have hle : X.basicOpen c ≤ X.basicOpen a.1 := by
    rw [← hac, hbo a]; exact inf_le_right
  rw [span_restrict_eq_top_of_le F (hV.basicOpen a.1) (hZ.basicOpen c) (a.2.trans hWV) hle A
    (hAspan a ha)]
  trivial

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01PFAffine

end
